02:06:07.500 --> 02:06:10.330
those people when they wake up the next morning,

2809
02:06:10.330 --> 02:06:12.330
they don't remember struggling to fall asleep.

2810
02:06:12.330 --> 02:06:14.260
They don't remember waking up,

2811
02:06:14.260 --> 02:06:15.470
frequently throughout the night,

2812
02:06:15.470 --> 02:06:17.450
so they don't put two and two together,

2813
02:06:17.450 --> 02:06:20.980
but now they feel unrefreshed and unrestored by their sleep

2814
02:06:20.980 --> 02:06:22.820
because they weren't getting the deep sleep.

2815
02:06:22.820 --> 02:06:23.940
And now they find themselves reaching for-

2816
02:06:23.940 --> 02:06:26.330
Gotta drink more caffeine.
Three cups of coffee

2817
02:06:26.330 --> 02:06:28.170
in the morning and then,

2818
02:06:28.170 --> 02:06:30.370
because they may not be able to get to sleep at night,

2819
02:06:30.370 --> 02:06:32.320
then they're reaching for sleeping pills.

2820
02:06:32.320 --> 02:06:34.260
So it's this sort of, you know,

2821
02:06:34.260 --> 02:06:36.090
it's the stimulant in the morning.

2822
02:06:36.090 --> 02:06:38.300
It's a sedative in the evening,

2823
02:06:38.300 --> 02:06:40.700
and it's a very difficult cycle to break.

2824
02:06:40.700 --> 02:06:42.183
So that's caffeine.

2825
02:06:43.490 --> 02:06:44.800
Alcohol.

2826
02:06:44.800 --> 02:06:48.030
Alcohol is probably the most misunderstood sleep aid

2827
02:06:48.030 --> 02:06:48.960
that there is out there.

2828
02:06:48.960 --> 02:06:50.860
It's anything but a sleep aid.

2829
02:06:50.860 --> 02:06:54.123
And, you've mentioned how your sleep was so disrupted.

2830
02:06:55.490 --> 02:06:57.530
First, the alcohol is in a class of drugs

2831
02:06:57.530 --> 02:06:59.350
that we call the sedatives.

2832
02:06:59.350 --> 02:07:02.060
And sedation is not sleep.

2833
02:07:02.060 --> 02:07:04.040
But when we have a couple of drinks in the evening

2834
02:07:04.040 --> 02:07:06.580
and we say, gosh, I've just fell asleep like that.

2835
02:07:06.580 --> 02:07:09.300
You're mistaking sedation for sleep.

2836
02:07:09.300 --> 02:07:11.440
So if I were to show you your electrical patterns

2837
02:07:11.440 --> 02:07:14.160
of brainwave activity with and without alcohol,

2838
02:07:14.160 --> 02:07:15.100
they're not the same.

2839
02:07:15.100 --> 02:07:18.800
It's not naturalistic brainwave activity.

2840
02:07:18.800 --> 02:07:20.530
The second problem with alcohol

2841
02:07:20.530 --> 02:07:22.770
is that it fragments your sleep

2842
02:07:22.770 --> 02:07:26.370
so that you wake up many more times throughout the night.

2843
02:07:26.370 --> 02:07:29.190
So not only is your sleep, you know,

2844
02:07:29.190 --> 02:07:31.660
going to be poor quality as we'll come on to.

2845
02:07:31.660 --> 02:07:33.410
It's also just not going to be consolidate,

2846
02:07:33.410 --> 02:07:35.760
it's not that little nice, long duration

2847
02:07:35.760 --> 02:07:37.540
of uninterrupted sleep.

2848
02:07:37.540 --> 02:07:41.690
Because as your body is processing the alcohol,

2849
02:07:41.690 --> 02:07:44.440
the depressant aspect of that drug is wearing off.

2850
02:07:44.440 --> 02:07:48.337
And there's a sort of rubber banding similar reaction to it.

2851
02:07:48.337 --> 02:07:51.000
So you wake up at two or three in the morning.

2852
02:07:51.000 --> 02:07:53.640
So it actually will start to just, as you mentioned there,

2853
02:07:53.640 --> 02:07:56.380
it will trigger activation of the fight or flight branch.

2854
02:07:56.380 --> 02:07:59.060
So you start to come back online in terms of that

2855
02:07:59.060 --> 02:08:01.740
stress related branch of the nervous system.

2856
02:08:01.740 --> 02:08:03.560
Also stress related neurochemicals,

2857
02:08:03.560 --> 02:08:06.840
we know are starting to get increased as the alcohol

2858
02:08:06.840 --> 02:08:07.710
is metabolized.

2859
02:08:07.710 --> 02:08:10.420
And that's what causes the fragmentation of your sleep.

2860
02:08:10.420 --> 02:08:12.530
The final problem with alcohol is that

2861
02:08:12.530 --> 02:08:15.782
it's a very potent suppressor of your REM sleep,

2862
02:08:15.782 --> 02:08:16.615
of your dream sleep.

2863
02:08:16.615 --> 02:08:19.160
Which we've mentioned before in terms of all its benefits.

2864
02:08:20.264 --> 02:08:21.813
And so, you know,

2865
02:08:21.813 --> 02:08:24.970
I think that's the reason that alcohol should just be

2866
02:08:24.970 --> 02:08:27.680
strongly advised against,

2867
02:08:27.680 --> 02:08:32.680
against the nightcap, by medical practitioners.

2868
02:08:32.820 --> 02:08:34.780
But I would just say two things, firstly,

2869
02:08:34.780 --> 02:08:36.840
with tongue-in-cheek, you know,

2870
02:08:36.840 --> 02:08:38.677
you could look at that data and say, well,

2871
02:08:38.677 --> 02:08:40.820
then I should just go to the pub in the morning.

2872
02:08:40.820 --> 02:08:42.920
And that way the alcohol is out of my system in the evening-

2873
02:08:42.920 --> 02:08:44.090
Now we're talking.

2874
02:08:44.090 --> 02:08:45.210
But yeah--
Problem with me is

2875
02:08:45.210 --> 02:08:46.550
if I go to the pub in the morning,

2876
02:08:46.550 --> 02:08:48.210
I'm at the pub at night too.

2877
02:08:48.210 --> 02:08:49.530
And so I would never say that

2878
02:08:49.530 --> 02:08:51.610
as a healthcare professional.

2879
02:08:51.610 --> 02:08:53.577
But what about like just a glass, like,

2880
02:08:53.577 --> 02:08:55.630
"Hey, I'm having a glass of wine at dinner."

2881
02:08:55.630 --> 02:08:57.694
Yeah, I would love say that,

2882
02:08:57.694 --> 02:09:00.812
based on the data that doesn't have an impact,

2883
02:09:00.812 --> 02:09:02.970
but if you look at the data even a glass

2884
02:09:02.970 --> 02:09:06.520
can have a measurable impact.

2885
02:09:06.520 --> 02:09:08.990
But look, the other thing I want to note is this

2886
02:09:08.990 --> 02:09:11.000
and I think it's something that I've learned in,

2887
02:09:11.000 --> 02:09:12.440
after the book was published.

2888
02:09:12.440 --> 02:09:15.723
And I'm embarrassed in the way I was acting before.

2889
02:09:17.350 --> 02:09:19.890
I don't wanna be puritanical here, Rich.

2890
02:09:19.890 --> 02:09:21.440
You know, I don't,

2891
02:09:21.440 --> 02:09:23.700
I don't want to tell people how to live their lives.

2892
02:09:23.700 --> 02:09:25.390
I'm just a scientist.

2893
02:09:25.390 --> 02:09:27.150
All I want to try and do

2894
02:09:27.150 --> 02:09:29.700
and I may be too enthusiastic in doing this

2895
02:09:29.700 --> 02:09:33.360
is gift people with the science and the knowledge of sleep.

2896
02:09:33.360 --> 02:09:35.480
And then they can make an empowered choice

2897
02:09:35.480 --> 02:09:37.520
as to how they want to live their life

2898
02:09:37.520 --> 02:09:40.090
if they're trying to optimize their sleep.

2899
02:09:40.090 --> 02:09:42.760
So I do want to mention that I am not finger-wagging

2900
02:09:42.760 --> 02:09:44.380
and I shouldn't be telling anyone--

2901
02:09:44.380 --> 02:09:46.540
I don't think anyone's getting that impression.

2902
02:09:46.540 --> 02:09:49.730
I think it's like, look, this is what's going on.

2903
02:09:49.730 --> 02:09:52.130
Like make your own, you know, choose accordingly.

2904
02:09:52.130 --> 02:09:55.010
But just so everybody knows, let's be clear about

2905
02:09:55.010 --> 02:09:57.860
what the science says in terms of how this impacts you.

2906
02:09:57.860 --> 02:10:01.610
Yeah, but I think I've been, sometimes overstep the mark.

2907
02:10:01.610 --> 02:10:03.580
You're such a gentle guy,

2908
02:10:03.580 --> 02:10:06.810
but I also should say like, I love how enthusiastic,

2909
02:10:06.810 --> 02:10:08.100
'cause you've talked about this stuff a lot,

2910
02:10:08.100 --> 02:10:09.820
but you're so enthusiastic.

2911
02:10:09.820 --> 02:10:12.799
Your whole body like lights up when you talk about

2912
02:10:12.799 --> 02:10:14.178
this stuff-
Oh my gosh.

2913
02:10:14.178 --> 02:10:18.210
It's the, it's the most, I fell in love with, you know,

2914
02:10:18.210 --> 02:10:20.100
I fell for sleep like a blind roof, you know,

2915
02:10:20.100 --> 02:10:23.160
it was just the most amazing thing

2916
02:10:23.160 --> 02:10:24.784
as I was starting to study it.

2917
02:10:24.784 --> 02:10:28.580
And it is a love affair that has lasted me 20 years.

2918
02:10:28.580 --> 02:10:31.230
And I am still beguiled by

2919
02:10:31.230 --> 02:10:33.563
this beautiful thing called sleep at night.

2920
02:10:35.266 --> 02:10:37.740
There's so much more still to be learned, right.

2921
02:10:37.740 --> 02:10:38.970
Like, you know.

2922
02:10:38.970 --> 02:10:40.795
I mean, it's, you know,

2923
02:10:40.795 --> 02:10:41.628
I think it's remains

2924
02:10:41.628 --> 02:10:42.680
one of the last great scientific mysteries.

2925
02:10:42.680 --> 02:10:45.070
I would say though, and the reason that at you're,

2926
02:10:45.070 --> 02:10:47.480
someone like me is able to write a book

2927
02:10:47.480 --> 02:10:51.100
that's over 130,000 words is because, you know,

2928
02:10:51.100 --> 02:10:53.830
we've learned more in the previous 50 years about sleep

2929
02:10:53.830 --> 02:10:56.370
than we did in the previous 5,000.

2930
02:10:56.370 --> 02:10:58.920
And even just 30 or 40 years ago,

2931
02:10:58.920 --> 02:11:02.450
we used to ask the question, what is sleep good for?

2932
02:11:02.450 --> 02:11:04.980
And the crass answer was that, well,

2933
02:11:04.980 --> 02:11:07.730
we sleep to cure sleepiness,

2934
02:11:07.730 --> 02:11:10.210
which is the factual equivalent of saying

2935
02:11:10.210 --> 02:11:11.890
we eat to cure hunger.

2936
02:11:11.890 --> 02:11:13.293
That tells you nothing about, you know,

2937
02:11:14.220 --> 02:11:18.793
the nutritional physiological metabolic benefits of food.

2938
02:11:19.660 --> 02:11:24.557
Now 30 or 40 years later, we've had to upend that question.

2939
02:11:24.557 --> 02:11:25.940
And we've had to ask,

2940
02:11:25.940 --> 02:11:29.630
is there any major organ system in your body

2941
02:11:29.630 --> 02:11:32.010
or is there any operation of the mind

2942
02:11:32.010 --> 02:11:34.730
that isn't wonderfully enhanced when we get sleep

2943
02:11:34.730 --> 02:11:37.890
or demonstrably impaired when we don't get enough?

2944
02:11:37.890 --> 02:11:39.390
And the answer seems to be no.

2945
02:11:40.810 --> 02:11:44.680
I have to ask you this, every full moon I don't sleep.

2946
02:11:44.680 --> 02:11:46.870
And I don't know if it's psychosomatic

2947
02:11:46.870 --> 02:11:50.300
or there's some kind of lunar gravitational pole occurring,

2948
02:11:50.300 --> 02:11:52.470
but have you looked at this?

2949
02:11:52.470 --> 02:11:53.303
We have.

2950
02:11:53.303 --> 02:11:54.170
Have you?
Yeah.

2951
02:11:54.170 --> 02:11:55.293
Please do tell.

2952
02:11:56.800 --> 02:11:58.440
There's some conflicting evidence.

2953
02:11:58.440 --> 02:12:00.690
So some reports have found this effect

2954
02:12:00.690 --> 02:12:02.343
other reports have not,

2955
02:12:03.360 --> 02:12:06.750
and it may be different for men and women even,

2956
02:12:06.750 --> 02:12:08.390
some of the reports are saying.

2957
02:12:08.390 --> 02:12:12.890
On average people sleep less with a full moon.

2958
02:12:12.890 --> 02:12:14.750
So if you ever thought about the term

2959
02:12:14.750 --> 02:12:17.303
or what the term means, lunatic.

2960
02:12:19.060 --> 02:12:22.110
And it occurred to me when I was doing that work

2961
02:12:22.110 --> 02:12:24.900
based on the relationship between sleep

2962
02:12:24.900 --> 02:12:27.050
and your emotional health, that you essentially,

2963
02:12:27.050 --> 02:12:29.400
your emotional integrity falls apart

2964
02:12:29.400 --> 02:12:31.200
when you're not getting sufficient sleep.

2965
02:12:31.200 --> 02:12:33.190
You become emotionally unhinged,

2966
02:12:33.190 --> 02:12:36.870
you become pendulum like in your emotional irrationality.

2967
02:12:36.870 --> 02:12:37.703
It occurred to me,

2968
02:12:37.703 --> 02:12:40.220
I wonder if part of the derivative of that term.

2969
02:12:40.220 --> 02:12:41.890
We've got all these things, the werewolf-

2970
02:12:41.890 --> 02:12:43.925
Well, it goes back forever.

2971
02:12:43.925 --> 02:12:46.950
Yeah. Like when the moon's out, people lose their minds.

2972
02:12:46.950 --> 02:12:50.090
Right. And you know, I think some of that is due to,

2973
02:12:50.090 --> 02:12:51.910
different practices around the celebration

2974
02:12:51.910 --> 02:12:53.570
of the moon phases, et cetera.

2975
02:12:53.570 --> 02:12:57.640
But I think if you believe some of the reports,

2976
02:12:57.640 --> 02:12:59.420
but again, some of the reports have fail

2977
02:12:59.420 --> 02:13:03.230
to find this effect, sleep duration decreases.

2978
02:13:03.230 --> 02:13:04.350
Why would that be?

2979
02:13:04.350 --> 02:13:05.800
There are some theories around that,

2980
02:13:05.800 --> 02:13:07.630
which actually I should finish up my tips

2981
02:13:07.630 --> 02:13:08.790
and there's just two more of them,

2982
02:13:08.790 --> 02:13:11.450
but this is nice because it brings us back to this.

2983
02:13:11.450 --> 02:13:13.070
With a full moon,

2984
02:13:13.070 --> 02:13:14.950
obviously, as long as it's not a cloudy night,

2985
02:13:14.950 --> 02:13:16.660
you get more luminance.

2986
02:13:16.660 --> 02:13:18.770
And that light of that luminance

2987
02:13:18.770 --> 02:13:23.180
can actually decrease the hormone of melatonin.

2988
02:13:23.180 --> 02:13:25.890
And this comes back to what, were I think the,

2989
02:13:25.890 --> 02:13:30.230
the fourth out of the five tips, which is darkness,

2990
02:13:30.230 --> 02:13:33.600
we are a dark society in this modern era

2991
02:13:33.600 --> 02:13:37.010
and we need darkness at night to trigger the release

2992
02:13:37.010 --> 02:13:39.490
of this hormone called melatonin.

2993
02:13:39.490 --> 02:13:43.860
And melatonin is often called sort of the vampire hormone.

2994
02:13:43.860 --> 02:13:46.080
Not because it makes you wanna look longingly

2995
02:13:46.080 --> 02:13:48.690
at people's neck lines an bite in,

2996
02:13:48.690 --> 02:13:50.310
it's because it comes out at night.

2997
02:13:50.310 --> 02:13:52.240
It's the hormone of darkness.

2998
02:13:52.240 --> 02:13:56.483
And melatonin helps time, the healthy onset of sleep.

2999
02:13:57.350 --> 02:14:00.660
And so the recommendation would be in the last hour

3000
02:14:00.660 --> 02:14:01.510
before bed,

3001
02:14:01.510 --> 02:14:05.480
don't just stay away from those blue light emitting devices,

3002
02:14:05.480 --> 02:14:09.370
try dimming down half the lights in your house.

3003
02:14:09.370 --> 02:14:11.970
You would actually be surprised at how sleepy

3004
02:14:11.970 --> 02:14:15.440
and soporific that change can be.

3005
02:14:15.440 --> 02:14:18.260
And that's why I love the idea of sleeping in a tent

3006
02:14:18.260 --> 02:14:23.180
because all of a sudden you are removed from all of that,

3007
02:14:23.180 --> 02:14:26.710
you know, polluting electric light even at night.

3008
02:14:26.710 --> 02:14:30.700
Now we should reverse engineer that trick during the day.

3009
02:14:30.700 --> 02:14:31.900
In the first half of the day,

3010
02:14:31.900 --> 02:14:36.400
it's critical to get some exposure to daylight.

3011
02:14:36.400 --> 02:14:37.550
You can go outside,

3012
02:14:37.550 --> 02:14:39.780
but it doesn't mean that you have to go outside

3013
02:14:39.780 --> 02:14:41.710
just being next to a window,

3014
02:14:41.710 --> 02:14:46.070
try to get at least 40 minutes of direct sunlight

3015
02:14:46.070 --> 02:14:48.440
each and every morning.

3016
02:14:48.440 --> 02:14:49.410
And that will really help

3017
02:14:49.410 --> 02:14:52.150
because that will then stamp the brakes on melatonin.

3018
02:14:52.150 --> 02:14:55.560
It will shut it down and you will feel more alert.

3019
02:14:55.560 --> 02:14:56.920
The more alert you feel,

3020
02:14:56.920 --> 02:15:00.220
the more healthy sleepiness, the more of that adenosine,

3021
02:15:00.220 --> 02:15:02.740
which is the sleep pressure chemical that you will build up

3022
02:15:02.740 --> 02:15:05.143
and then the better your sleep will be at night.

3023
02:15:05.990 --> 02:15:07.830
So that's sort of darkness

3024
02:15:07.830 --> 02:15:10.290
and I think that's perhaps part of the explanation

3025
02:15:10.290 --> 02:15:13.090
why the full moon can maybe disrupt our sleep

3026
02:15:13.090 --> 02:15:15.390
because it's nowhere near like sunlight,

3027
02:15:15.390 --> 02:15:17.180
but it's still a light invasion.

3028
02:15:17.180 --> 02:15:19.843
But I wear the eye mask and the whole thing.

3029
02:15:21.006 --> 02:15:22.590
I think there's something more mysterious at play.

3030
02:15:22.590 --> 02:15:24.560
I don't know, but maybe I'll try taking melatonin.

3031
02:15:24.560 --> 02:15:26.720
I know that you've said, you know,

3032
02:15:26.720 --> 02:15:28.443
taking melatonin as a matter of course,

3033
02:15:28.443 --> 02:15:29.520
it's not a good idea.

3034
02:15:29.520 --> 02:15:33.070
It's really for when you're traveling across time zones,

3035
02:15:33.070 --> 02:15:37.301
but maybe I'll try it when the next full moon cycle comes.

3036
02:15:37.301 --> 02:15:38.480
(indistinct)
Yeah you can try it.

3037
02:15:38.480 --> 02:15:40.900
I mean, melatonin, as I mentioned,

3038
02:15:40.900 --> 02:15:43.450
it regulates the timing of your sleep,

3039
02:15:43.450 --> 02:15:45.030
but it doesn't actually really help

3040
02:15:45.030 --> 02:15:46.570
in the generation of sleep.

3041
02:15:46.570 --> 02:15:50.030
If you look at people who are not jet lagged

3042
02:15:50.030 --> 02:15:52.650
and who are under the age of 50,

3043
02:15:52.650 --> 02:15:55.240
melatonin and all of the placebo controlled cities

3044
02:15:55.240 --> 02:15:57.170
that we found doesn't really change

3045
02:15:57.170 --> 02:16:00.260
the quantity or the quality of your sleep.

3046
02:16:00.260 --> 02:16:02.839
Melatonin, you can think of it a little bit like,

3047
02:16:02.839 --> 02:16:06.420
the starting official at the 100 meter race.

3048
02:16:06.420 --> 02:16:09.620
Melatonin is the thing that will gather all of the,

3049
02:16:09.620 --> 02:16:13.460
the races to the start and then begin the great sleep race.

3050
02:16:13.460 --> 02:16:16.500
But melatonin doesn't participate in the race itself

3051
02:16:16.500 --> 02:16:19.600
that's a whole different set of brain chemicals.

3052
02:16:19.600 --> 02:16:22.623
But I would say two things regarding melatonin.

3053
02:16:23.520 --> 02:16:27.083
First, if you think that it's working for you,

3054
02:16:28.060 --> 02:16:30.570
then the placebo effect is the most reliable effect

3055
02:16:30.570 --> 02:16:32.900
in all of pharmacology, with the exception

3056
02:16:32.900 --> 02:16:35.400
of probably an adrenaline injection to your heart.

3057
02:16:36.670 --> 02:16:38.513
So no harm, no foul there.

3058
02:16:39.478 --> 02:16:42.300
The caveat that I would like to add to that secondarily

3059
02:16:42.300 --> 02:16:44.440
is, it's over the counter

